# ============================================================
# You_can React Frontend Environment Configuration
# ============================================================
#
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT:
# When developing locally with Vite (`npm run dev`), the Vite dev server
# automatically proxies all `/api/*` requests to http://127.0.0.1:8080.
# No environment variables are required for local development.
#
# VERCEL PRODUCTION DEPLOYMENT:
# In Vercel, API requests are proxied via `vercel.json` rewrites to your
# deployed Java Spring Boot backend.
#
# Step 1: Deploy your Spring Boot backend to any Java-compatible host
#         (e.g., Render, Railway, AWS ECS, GCP Cloud Run, Heroku).
# Step 2: In vercel.json, replace `https://BACKEND_API_URL_PLACEHOLDER` with
#         your actual deployed backend URL (e.g., `https://youcan-api.onrender.com`).
# Step 3: On your backend host, set the environment variable:
#         APP_CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://your-vercel-domain.vercel.app
#
# The browser navigates exclusively to your Vercel domain, and Vercel
# seamlessly proxies API calls to the backend, preserving the single-URL
# user experience and session cookies.
# ============================================================
